🔐 OAUTH 2.0 SETUP GUIDE: Secure API Integration with Anaplan
  - This guide walks you through the OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials Grant setup in Anaplan to enable secure, 
    service-account–based authentication for integrations (e.g., with Snowflake, AWS Lambda, Azure, Boomi, Python scripts, etc.)

🧭 1. Overview of OAuth 2.0 in Anaplan
  - Grant Type Used: Client Credentials (non-interactive, for system-to-system)
  - Use Case: Replaces Basic Auth for automated jobs (data integrations, CI/CD jobs)
  - Actors Involved:
    - Client App (external system calling Anaplan API)
    - Authorization Server (Anaplan)
    - Resource Server (Anaplan REST API)

📋 2. Prerequisites
  - Workspace Admin privileges in Anaplan
  - Access to the Anaplan Administration Console
  - A user account tied to a Service Principal (no interactive logins)
  - External integration platform (e.g., Postman, Python, Boomi, or Anaplan Connect)

⚙️ 3. Step-by-Step Setup Instructions
  🔧 Step 1: Register a New Integration Client
      1) Go to Anaplan Admin Console
      2) Navigate to Authentication > Integration Clients
      3) Click "Add Integration Client"
      4) Fill in the required fields:
        - Name: My_Snowflake_Integration
        - Description: Snowflake to Anaplan OAUTH2 connection
        - Authentication Method: OAuth 2.0
      5) Copy and securely store the generated:
        - Client ID
        - Client Secret
        - Token URL: https://auth.anaplan.com/token/authenticate
    
  🔑 Step 2: Assign the Integration Client to a User
    1) Go to Access Control > Users
    2) Select a user to act as the Service Principal
    3) Under Authentication Methods, click Add Integration Client
    4) Assign the newly created Client ID
    5) Save
  🔒 This user must have appropriate Workspace/Model roles for any data access
  
  🧪 Step 3: Test OAuth Token Retrieval (Postman Example)
    Set POST request to:
      - https://auth.anaplan.com/token/authenticate
      - Set Body → x-www-form-urlencoded:
          grant_type=client_credentials
          client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
          client_secret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET
      - Click Send
      
      Response will include:
        {
          "token_type": "Bearer",
          "expires_in": 3600,
          "access_token": "eyJ0eXAiOiJK..."
        }
  
  📡 Step 4: Use Access Token in Anaplan API Calls
    - Add the access token to the Authorization header for all Anaplan API requests:
      Authorization: Bearer eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhb...
  
    - Example GET request to list workspaces:  
      GET https://api.anaplan.com/2/0/workspaces
      Authorization: Bearer eyJ0eXAiOiJK...

🔁 4. Token Management Best Practices
  - Token expiration: 1 hour (3600 seconds)
  - Use automation to refresh token before expiry
  - Never hard-code credentials — use secrets management tools (e.g., AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault)
  - Log token generation attempts for auditing

🧰 5. Python Script Example
  import requests
  
  def get_access_token(client_id, client_secret):
      url = 'https://auth.anaplan.com/token/authenticate'
      data = {
          'grant_type': 'client_credentials',
          'client_id': client_id,
          'client_secret': client_secret
      }
      response = requests.post(url, data=data)
      return response.json()['access_token']
  
  token = get_access_token('YOUR_CLIENT_ID', 'YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET')
  headers = {'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'}
  resp = requests.get('https://api.anaplan.com/2/0/workspaces', headers=headers)
  print(resp.json())

🧠 6. Troubleshooting Tips
  Error                    |  Likely Cause                                 | 	Fix
  401 Unauthorized         |  Invalid client credentials or expired token  |  Regenerate token
  403 Forbidden            |  User lacks model/workspace access            |  Check roles in Anaplan
  Invalid client           |  Client ID not assigned to user               |  Re-check Admin Console assignment
  unsupported_grant_type   |  Typo in grant_type or wrong content type     |  Should be client_credentials

🛡️ 7. Security Considerations
  - Rotate client secrets periodically
  - Lock down Anaplan access to specific roles
  - Disable unused OAuth clients
  - Audit token generation and API usage logs

✅ 8. Checklist Summary
  ✅ Item	Description
    🔲	Registered integration client in Anaplan
    🔲	Assigned client to a service user
    🔲	Confirmed correct workspace/model access
    🔲	Tested token generation and API call
    🔲	Implemented automated token refresh process
